{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9f1c2a4e-7b3d-4c58-9e60-1a2b3c4d5e6f",
    "name": "Franchise Inventory API",
    "description": "Requests for the Franchise Inventory API, mirroring the smoke test walkthrough in the README.\n\n**Format:** Postman Collection v2.1, importable by Postman, Insomnia and Bruno.\n\n**Order:** run the folders top to bottom. `1. Smoke test walkthrough` creates the franchise, two branches, two products, raises a stock and reads the top-stock report. `2. Error contract` reuses the ids created in folder 1.\n\n**Authentication:** every business route needs HTTP Basic with the local dev API Credential, set at collection level from the `apiUsername` and `apiPassword` variables. The collection defaults are the local dev pair: never use them outside local development. The health and 401 requests override this (no auth).\n\n**Variables:** `baseUrl` defaults to http://localhost:8080. Ids are URL path variables (`:franchiseId`, `:downtownBranchId`, `:uptownBranchId`, `:cheeseburgerId`, `:friesId`), each backed by a collection variable of the same name. The test scripts in Postman fill those variables from the create responses; in Insomnia and Bruno, copy the returned ids into the variables after each create request. `suffix` is a collection variable used in request bodies; set it to a new value (for example `-2`) before rerunning against a database that already has `Burger Town`, because franchise names are unique case-insensitively.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "basic",
    "basic": [
      {
        "key": "username",
        "value": "{{apiUsername}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "password",
        "value": "{{apiPassword}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
